.\" our-dots.1 — man page for our-dots v0.6.1
.TH OUR-DOTS 1 "2026-06-08" "ouroborOS v0.6.1" "ouroborOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
our-dots \- dotfiles/config pack manager for ouroborOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B our-dots
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B our-dots
installs and manages curated ricing packs (dotfiles, shell configs, and
desktop environment configurations) on top of installed ouroborOS desktop
profiles.
Packs are YAML manifests shipped with the ISO or provided by external
repositories.
.PP
The tool enforces compatibility with the immutable root filesystem
(Btrfs, read-only).
Packs marked
.B CRITICAL
require explicit confirmation or the
.I OUROBOROS_ALLOW_CRITICAL=1
environment variable for unattended installs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Display all available packs in a tabular view (name, desktop environment,
compatibility level, available channels, installed status).
.TP
.BI \-Si " pack"
Show detailed information about
.IR pack :
description, author, homepage, compatibility level, and available channels.
.TP
.BI \-S " pack " [ \-\-git ] [ \-\-noconfirm ] [ \-\-force ]
Install
.IR pack .
By default the
.I stable
channel is used.
Pass
.B \-\-git
to install the git (rolling) channel.
.TP
.BI \-R " pack " [ \-\-noconfirm ] [ \-\-force ]
Remove
.IR pack
and run its
.I post_remove
script if defined.
.TP
.B \-Q
List all installed packs with their installed version and date.
.TP
.BI \-Qs " [pattern]"
Search the full catalog by name or description.
If
.I pattern
is omitted, all packs are listed.
.TP
.B \-Su
Check installed packs for updates via the AUR API and reinstall any that have
a newer version available.
Packs with
.I compatibility=critical
are skipped and must be upgraded manually.
.TP
.BI repo\-add " name url"
Register an external manifest repository.
.I url
must use HTTPS.
Git repositories and HTTP index files are both supported.
All fetched manifests are validated against the canonical schema before the
repo is registered.
.TP
.BI repo\-remove " name"
Remove an external repository and delete its cached manifests.
.TP
.B repo\-list
List all configured repositories (built-in and external).
.TP
.B repo\-update
Fetch the latest manifests from all registered external repositories.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-noconfirm
Skip interactive confirmation prompts.
Cannot bypass
.B CRITICAL
confirmation unless
.I OUROBOROS_ALLOW_CRITICAL=1
is also set.
.TP
.B \-\-git
Install the git (rolling/development) channel variant of a pack.
Automatically set for packs that only have a
.I variants.git
block (git-only packs).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip "already installed" check during install or "not installed" check during removal.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.I "our-dots <version>"
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set (to any value), disable ANSI color output.
Follows the
.I no-color.org
convention.
.TP
.B OUROBOROS_ALLOW_CRITICAL=1
Allow unattended installation of packs with
.I compatibility=critical
.
When set,
.B \-\-noconfirm
is accepted without the interactive "yes" prompt.
Used by the installer (configure.sh) and for scripted deployments.
.SH COMPATIBILITY LEVELS
.TP
.B low
Pack installs entirely in user space (AUR packages, \fI~/.config\fP).
No system changes.
.TP
.B medium
Pack modifies user config but may install pacman packages.
.TP
.B high
Pack has significant system-level impact (long AUR builds, system font changes,
etc.).
Requires interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B CRITICAL
Pack modifies read-only system files (\fI/etc/pacman.conf\fP,
bootloader preferences, etc.).
Requires typing
.I yes
or setting
.IR OUROBOROS_ALLOW_CRITICAL=1 .
A cleanup trap reverts system changes on failure and exits with code
.IR 5 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/ouroboros/dots/packs/
Built-in pack manifest directory.
Each \fI<id>.yaml\fP file defines a pack.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ouroboros/dots/repos/
External repository cache directory.
.TP
.I /etc/ouroboros/dots\-repos.yaml
Registered external repositories index.
.TP
.I /etc/ouroboros/system.yaml
System state file.
The
.I dots_packs
list records installed packs with version, channel, date, and origin.
.TP
.I /var/log/our-dots/
Per-pack install logs.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (unknown command, cancelled by user, not found).
.TP
.B 2
Root privileges required.
.TP
.B 3
AUR package installation failed.
.TP
.B 4
post_deploy script failed.
.TP
.B 5
CRITICAL install failed; system changes were reverted by the cleanup trap.
.SH EXAMPLES
List available packs:
.PP
.RS
.B our-dots list
.RE
.PP
Show info for the ml4w pack:
.PP
.RS
.B our-dots \-Si ml4w
.RE
.PP
Install noctalia from the stable channel:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo our-dots \-S noctalia
.RE
.PP
Install illogical-impulse (git-only, CRITICAL):
.PP
.RS
.B sudo our-dots \-S illogical-impulse
.RE
.PP
Install with unattended CRITICAL bypass (for the installer):
.PP
.RS
.B OUROBOROS_ALLOW_CRITICAL=1 sudo our-dots \-S illogical-impulse \-\-noconfirm
.RE
.PP
Remove a pack:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo our-dots \-R noctalia
.RE
.PP
Add an external manifest repository:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo our-dots repo-add myrepo https://github.com/example/dots-repo.git
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR our-pac (1),
.BR our-aur (1),
.BR pacman (8)
.SH AUTHORS
ouroborOS dev team.
Pack authors and credits are listed in each pack manifest
.RI ( credits.author ,
.IR credits.homepage ).
